   one satellite are DIFFERENT ROWS. BOTH SCOPES are quoted below because a
   bare writer count overstates the arbitrariness -- on PARTY_FULL_NAME it
   overstates it nearly fivefold.
   DECLARED, NOT RESOLVED: choosing among same-run writers would invent an
   authority the map does not provide. NO CROSS-RUN DECISION REACHES THIS.
     CHEQUE_DATE                            opus_health_legacy_v4  2 writer(s), of which 2 UNDISCRIMINATED (0 separated by a resolved instance, 0 by redundant_of)  [CROSS-TABLE: check_collapse groups on (table, satellite, attribute, instance, child_key) and CANNOT see this]
     NET_PAID_AMOUNT                        opus_health_legacy_v4  4 writer(s), of which 1 UNDISCRIMINATED (3 separated by a resolved instance, 0 by redundant_of)
     TDS_ON_CLAIM_AMOUNT                    opus_health_legacy_v4  3 writer(s), of which 3 UNDISCRIMINATED (0 separated by a resolved instance, 0 by redundant_of)  [CROSS-TABLE: check_collapse groups on (table, satellite, attribute, instance, child_key) and CANNOT see this]
   A load-time assertion in models/assertions/ counts the DISTINCT
